      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of H2L (0.1 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.1 mmol), MnC2O4 (0.05 mmol), NaOH (0.2 mmol), MeOH (1.5 mL), and DMF (0.5 mL) was sealed in a Pyrex tube (10 mL) and heated at 80 °C for 48 h. After cooling to room temperature, block-shaped crystals of 1 were obtained. HCOOH, μ4-O2−, and H3L' were generated in situ; MnC2O4 catalyzes oxidation of MeOH to formate.",
